virglrenderer: Venus logs a refusal's reason whole

What: the reason buffers of vkCreateShaderModule, vkCreateGraphicsPipelines and
vkCreateComputePipelines, and the line vkr_context_refuse formats, take 512 bytes (were
192 and 256), and every byte below 0x20 in that line's reason and context name becomes a
space (the name on a copy of up to 127 bytes: other lines and the GPU guard keep
ctx->debug_name as it is).
Nothing else changes: the same checks, the same refusals.
Why: spirv-val's message for one module runs to about 300 characters with the
"spirv-val (SPIR-V 1.6 (under Vulkan 1.4 semantics)): " prefix and the instruction it
names. 192 cut it in qemu.log (#710: "... the Function storage class has a ex"), so
the reason a context ended was not readable. Whole, the message puts the instruction and
"(word N)" on lines of their own; one refusal stays one line. The guest's names reach the
line too: spirv-val quotes string literals (an entry point's name) as they are, vkr's own
"no entry point" reason quotes the stage's pName, and the context name is the app's
process name. A CR, ESC or newline there split the line or rewrote it on a terminal
(#718). Compared as unsigned char: char is signed on arm64, so a plain compare would also
blank UTF-8. DEL (0x7f) and C1 controls (0x80-0x9f, in UTF-8 C2 80-9F) are left as they
are on purpose: the item is one line per refusal, and UTF-8 names keep their letters.
Upstream: no (OmacVM's own checks).
Tests: build-qemu-gpu-runtime.sh checks the four buffers and both loops after the patch;
test-venus-commands.c's p-entry-name-ctl (a pName with CR, ESC, TAB) and p-ctx-name-ctl
(a context name with them and a newline), and every refusal case checks its line has no
byte below 0x20 but its own newline; the long message in qemu.log was seen whole in a
test VM (#710).

diff --git a/src/venus/vkr_context.c b/src/venus/vkr_context.c
--- a/src/venus/vkr_context.c
+++ b/src/venus/vkr_context.c
@@ -600,11 +600,23 @@
 
    /* the 1st, 2nd, 4th, 8th ... refusal: a guest in a loop cannot flood the log */
    if (!(n & (n - 1))) {
-      char why[256];
+      char why[512]; /* OmacVM (virgl-venus-refusal-text.patch) */
       va_list va;
       va_start(va, fmt);
       vsnprintf(why, sizeof(why), fmt, va);
       va_end(va);
+      /* spirv-val's lines and the guest's names (the app's, a shader's entry point): one
+       * refusal, one line, no control bytes; unsigned, so UTF-8 stays (char is signed on arm64) */
+      char name[128];
+      snprintf(name, sizeof(name), "%s", ctx->debug_name ? ctx->debug_name : "?");
+      for (char *c = why; *c; c++) {
+         if ((unsigned char)*c < 0x20)
+            *c = ' ';
+      }
+      for (char *c = name; *c; c++) {
+         if ((unsigned char)*c < 0x20)
+            *c = ' ';
+      }
       vkr_log("%s: %s refused: %s%s (%" PRIu64 " refused so far)",
-              ctx->debug_name ? ctx->debug_name : "?", call, why,
+              name, call, why,
               fatal ? "; the app's Vulkan context ends" : "", n);
